## ✍️ 2.8 Comments and Indentation
- **Line Comment (`//`):** Used to add a brief explanatory note on a single line of code.
- **Block Comment (`/* ... */`):** Used to write longer, multi-line explanations across consecutive lines.
- **Indentation:** Structuring blocks with empty lines and proper spacing ensures the code remains highly human-readable.

---

## 🚪 2.9 Closing a Form
To close the currently active user interface form or shutdown an application window via code, use this statement:

```csharp
private void exitButton_Click(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    // Closes the active form instance
    this.Close(); 
}
```

---

## ⚠️ 2.10 Dealing with Syntax Errors
- **Syntax Error:** A mistake that occurs when your code violates the grammar and structure rules of the C# language.
- Visual Studio reports these errors instantly by highlighting the problematic code with a red wavy **jagged line**. The program cannot compile or run successfully until all syntax errors are completely resolved.